  "number": "2.4",
  "title": "Lie’s Third Theorem",
  "body": " Lie's Third Theorem  In this section we introduce closed subgroups of Lie groups. As usual, we start with understanding the closed subgroups for matrix groups, extract their properties and then construct and analyze the formal object.  ` Lie Subgroup   A Lie subgroup of a Lie group is a subgroup that is also an immersed submanifold of .     Lie's Third Theorem   Distribution   If is a smooth manifold, then an -dimensional smooth distribution is a smooth association of each point an -dimensional subspace of . In otherwords, it section into the Grassman bundle .     Involutive Distribution   If is a smooth manifold, then an -dimensional involutive distribution is a smooth distribution such that for any two vector fields , their Lie bracket is also in .      If is a Lie group and is a Lie subalgebra, then defines an involutive distribution on .     Involutive Distributions are Integrable  Frobenius   If is a smooth manifold and is an involutive distribution, then there exists a unique maximal integral manifold such that .     Lie's Third Theorem   If is a Lie group and is a Lie subalgebra, then there exists a connected immersed Lie subgroup of with Lie algebra .         "
